{
 "schema": "barviews-clips-1",
 "what": "video clips of the bar's episodes and of the frozen references: views, no verdict, nothing adopted",
 "labels": {
  "simulated": "SIMULATION (physics)",
  "planned": "PLANNED MOTION (kinematic, no physics)"
 },
 "rules": {
  "selection": "which episode a clip shows (stated before any record existed): the block's first seed; if that episode's outcome (stayed up or fell) is not the majority outcome of the record's episodes, in addition the lowest seed with the majority outcome whose trace is kept.  An episode that failed to run has no outcome and no clip.  On a tie the first seed's outcome counts as the majority.  A trace that was not kept, is missing or does not have the record's sha256 gives no clip; the manifest says why",
  "span": "a clip starts 1 s before the command and ends 1 s after the end of the move (a turn: the end of its own file on the reference clock, read from the trace; a stop: the planned rest; a nudge: the pulse's end plus the bar's recovery limit) or at the trace's end if that comes first; a walk: the first 10 s of its judged window.  An episode that fell: the clip runs to the fall instant the record gives and the last recorded pose is held for 1 s under the caption 'fell' (a trace ends at the fall); if it fell before its command, or a walk before its judged window, the clip is the last 4 s before the fall (a walk: up to 10 s)",
  "time": "30 frames a second at real time: frame k shows the simulated time t0 + k / 30 s; between the 50 Hz rows the root position and the joint angles are interpolated linearly and the root's quaternion by normalised linear interpolation (clips.Playback's rule)",
  "pose": "simulated: pose_of on the episode's trace (module docstring: exact attitude and root, the height from the feet's low points, the joint angles moved back one physics step); planned: the frozen reference played kinematically at the bar's commanded clock",
  "cameras": "visitor and side: clips.CAMERAS' eye height, distance and bearing, the bearing counted from the incoming walking line and kept for the whole clip; the look-at point follows the planned root path (the reference at the reference time the episode's own clock has reached, so that the clock's play does not move the picture), averaged over one stride, moved to the body's bounding box centre as it lies from the root at home and at that centre's height.  A simulated clip moves that path by one constant for the whole clip: the mean, over the clip's seconds, of the simulated root's place from its planned place (a robot that drifted off its plan before the clip is then still in the picture). Within a clip the cameras do not follow the body: not its wobble, and not a drift from the plan during the clip, which shows as the robot leaving the picture's centre.  top: a fixed eye straight above the middle of the clip's sweep, high enough to hold it, the picture's up along the incoming walking line, the headlight's diffuse part lowered to 0.2 (straight down the model's own washes the floor out)",
  "labels": "first line of every frame: 'SIMULATION (physics)' or 'PLANNED MOTION (kinematic, no physics)', never both, the body and the set; second line: the condition and the row in plain words; bottom: seed, this episode's outcome, the record's count, the view, the clip time.  From the command, for 1.5 s: 'command: ...' (read from the record); from the fall instant: 'fell'",
  "media": "854 x 480, H.264 through clips.encode, at most 3000000 bytes each; a poster and a contact sheet (the frames at 1/8, 3/8, 5/8 and 7/8 of the clip) beside each; the media are written outside git and listed here with their sha256"
 },
 "run": "stage2/runs/2026-11-15-75cm",
 "media_dir": "outside git (the --media directory of the run; files relative to it)",
